        <p class="postingContent">
            <p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial;">Candidates must meet the minimum qualifications for the Administrative Law Judge classification and have certification (reachable) list eligibility, transfer eligibility, reinstatement rights, SROA, and/or Surplus eligibility (attach letter if applicable) or reinstatement rights.</span></span></p><p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial;">&nbsp;</span></span></p><p style="font-size: 11pt; text-align: left; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial;">Candidates who have list eligibility (or are in the process of obtaining list eligibility) may also apply. To obtain list eligibility, please review the following list bulletin: <a href="https://calcareers.ca.gov/CalHrPublic/Exams/ExamBulletin.aspx?ExamControlId=1507" style="text-decoration: none;"><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><span style="color: #0000ff;">Administrative Law Judge</span></span></a></span></span></p><p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial;">&nbsp;</span></span></p><p style="font-size: 11pt; text-align: left; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial;">Candidates must meet the Minimum Qualifications stated in this <a href="https://www.calhr.ca.gov/state-hr-professionals/Pages/6016.aspx" style="text-decoration: none;"><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><span style="color: #0000ff;">Classification Specification(s)</span></span></a></span><span style="font-family: Arial;">.</span></span></p><p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"></span></p>
